t {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250432} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fc2c1ee-5fd8-59cf-97ff-a46de525b2f3" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4dac05e-84dd-5a26-905f-fb4d126dc4c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11556" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$T=\\begin{bmatrix}1.5 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $3$ rows and $2$ columns, so it's a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $S$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $T$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $5$ rows and $5$ columns, so it is a $5\\times 5$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $S$ and $T$ are square matrices." :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568891 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250432} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 13.378 :task-item/id #uuid "29983756-59c7-4587-bfdb-ce814970f0e4" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568892} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "66d0ae76-bc3f-5fc2-ab45-3c327cc7dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461737} {:answer/id #uuid "d62d551d-96da-517f-8340-2d16b1ab916d" :answer/type {:db/id #